## Product-specific anti-patterns

- Do not fabricate customer testimonials, ratings, savings, prices, or comparison results.
- Do not present unverified claims, dates, forecasts, or performance metrics as facts.
- Do not publish testimonials without permission to use the quoted content and visual assets.
- Do not use broken, distorted, cropped, or unreadable logos.
- Do not make the logo link to an invalid, empty, or unrelated destination.
- Do not hide, disable, or place the primary CTA outside the normal content flow.
- Do not send CTA clicks to an error page, blank page, or unrelated service.
- Do not change the CTA destination without explicit approval.
- Do not let text, images, testimonials, or CTA buttons overlap or leave the viewport.
- Do not reorder core content and CTA elements in a way that disrupts the same journey across mobile and desktop.
- Do not use unsupported browser-specific behavior for essential content or CTA interactions.
- Do not use duplicate, misleading, or content-inconsistent SEO titles and descriptions.
- Do not set a canonical URL to an unapproved or non-representative domain.
- Do not configure page language or search directives that conflict with the actual Korean content.
- Do not block page rendering when visit or CTA analytics fail.
- Do not record duplicate visit or CTA-click events for a single interaction.
- Do not claim that analytics are active unless visit and CTA-click events are verifiably recorded.
<!-- TBD: The analytics provider and approved event schema are not specified in the profile. -->
- Do not deploy to production or connect a live service domain without an explicit request.

## Universal guardrails

- Do not invent features, screens, or API endpoints that are absent from `docs/PRD.md`.
- Do not silently change the folder structure declared in `01-architecture.mdc`.
- Do not introduce a dependency without updating PRD §10 Tech Stack in the same commit.
- Do not add signup fields, inquiry forms, pricing tools, comparison tools, or account flows unless explicitly required.
- Do not add an internationalization framework or locale switcher.
- Do not mix languages in source code, code comments, or generated documentation.
- Do not use non-Korean user-facing copy unless explicitly requested.
- Do not remove responsive behavior, SEO metadata, testimonials, CTA navigation, or required analytics.
- Do not suppress errors that prevent required content or interactions from working.
- Do not weaken accessibility with unlabeled controls, keyboard-inaccessible CTAs, or unreadable contrast.
- Do not add production deployment configuration without explicit approval.

## Secrets & PII

- Do not hardcode API keys, secrets, analytics credentials, tokens, or payment keys.
- Do not commit `.env` files containing secrets.
- Do not expose secrets through client-side bundles, HTML, metadata, URLs, logs, or analytics payloads.
- Do not collect personal information that is unnecessary for signup, service start, or inquiry completion.
- Do not place names, phone numbers, email addresses, account identifiers, or inquiry details in URLs.
- Do not send testimonial authors’ personal information to analytics.
- Do not log form contents, contact details, or free-text inquiry content.
- Do not use real customer data in fixtures, screenshots, demos, or automated tests.
- Do not publish identifiable testimonial details without documented consent.
- Do not track sensitive or directly identifying data in visit or CTA-click events.
- Do not store consent or inquiry data longer than an approved retention period.
